objective:
Please deploy this repository as it is: contracts only, on Ethereum mainnet. There is no token and no owner.

It holds three contracts, to be created in this order: Rules, Endowments, Zap. Their constructor arguments are in docs/LAUNCH.md: ten addresses in all, every one a literal. Three are existing mainnet contracts (IMD, the sIMD staking vault and Uniswap's v4 PoolManager) and three are contracts of our two earlier launches, live since 13 October 2026: Questions (0xEECE4628ceb091C13393fc64056Be8b8501fD3F6) of launch 1531, and WorkOrders (0x730CB6C845d896e33283d3A4Ed8967F8BAA778d2) and CrowdPots (0x8C2FfCdcb103659aa05c772b8F2059868B496EB5) of launch 1573. Some are given to more than one contract. No contract of this launch refers to another, so there is no $contract: reference, and no argument is $owner: no contract has an owner, an admin or a setter.

Nothing has to be called after deployment. The constructors make no external call and check no code size, so they run on an empty chain. There is no proxy, no initializer, no pausing and no minting; the runtime bytecode holds no DELEGATECALL, CALLCODE or SELFDESTRUCT. Zap has three functions that take ETH, because paying with ETH is what it is for; deployment sends none. forge test checks each of these statements (test/launch/LaunchC.t.sol).

The project builds with solc 0.8.26, EVM version cancun, optimizer 200 runs, via_ir, bytecode_hash = "none" and cbor_metadata = false, as foundry.toml already says. We believe no source file needs to change for the launch. The folder integration/ is a second Foundry project that tests these contracts against the sources of our earlier launches; forge build, forge test and forge fmt --check run from the root do not reach it, it builds only beside those two repositories, and it is not part of what is deployed. docs/THREATS.md, section 10, says what we checked in this code after the changes your pipeline made to our first launch and the findings your auditors raised on our second, and why each rule here is as it is.

One sentence on two rules we ask you to leave as they are: Rules.fire pays a rule's tip to whoever fires it first, and Endowments.harvest, open to anyone, sends yield only to the target the endowment's creator fixed, a contract included, because there is no earlier party to pay instead and no other address the money may go to (docs/THREATS.md, section 10, patterns 1 to 3).

The manifest we expect (also in docs/LAUNCH.md, where a test checks it against the code):
{
 "kind": "evm_contracts",
 "contracts": [
  {
   "contract": "Rules",
   "constructorArgs": [
    "0xd34a99bc0f67ae1bbd63c660e6d0b0dd03e263b7",
    "0x730cb6c845d896e33283d3a4ed8967f8baa778d2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "contract": "Endowments",
   "constructorArgs": [
    "0xd34a99bc0f67ae1bbd63c660e6d0b0dd03e263b7",
    "0x9efa934d9fad4ae28c998a40195646b965a97247",
    "0xeece4628ceb091c13393fc64056be8b8501fd3f6",
    "0x8c2ffcdcb103659aa05c772b8f2059868b496eb5"
   ]
  },
  {
   "contract": "Zap",
   "constructorArgs": [
    "0xd34a99bc0f67ae1bbd63c660e6d0b0dd03e263b7",
    "0x000000000004444c5dc75cb358380d2e3de08a90",
    "0x8c2ffcdcb103659aa05c772b8f2059868b496eb5",
    "0xeece4628ceb091c13393fc64056be8b8501fd3f6"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "notes": "Contracts only. No token, no owner, nothing to call after deployment. Three arguments are contracts of our two earlier launches: WorkOrders and CrowdPots of launch 1573 and Questions of launch 1531."
}

